From 51b9f319276f8922c1e529010a64f2184fb5c0a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/34] usb_webcam: add an MJPEG decoder and a frame list for
 UVC

Two building blocks for MJPEG, which the next change puts to use:

UVCFrameList.h builds one list of sizes from the frame descriptors of
all formats: for each size the faster format, the uncompressed one at
the same rate, sorted by area and capped at 32 entries. Each entry
keeps its own format and frame index for the probe.

UVCJpegDecoder decodes a frame with libjpeg-turbo straight into
B_RGB32. Errors are caught, and a damaged frame, which libjpeg only
reports as a warning, is dropped. The size and the output buffer are
checked once before decoding. Frames without Huffman tables, as the
built-in camera of a ThinkPad T470s sends them, get the standard
tables from libjpeg.

UVCFrameListTest and UVCJpegDecoderTest cover both; the decoder test
encodes its own small frames, also one without Huffman tables.
Decoding a 1920x1080 frame of a Logitech C920 takes 8 ms on an
i7-7500U.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 885226f1c6d6426bf58f1a29da97169ed38b8118)
